<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal plans 300 bln escudo motorway expansion.</title>
<headline>Portugal plans 300 bln escudo motorway expansion.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal plans to build 730 kms (460 miles) of new motorway by the end of the year 2000 in a series of projects worth some 307 billion escudos, a spokesman for the Planning and Public Works Ministry said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said that minister Joao Cravinho would present proposals for the launching of international tenders for the projects at next week's cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>The motorways would be toll-free, the spokesman added, with the state paying the concession-winner a fee to be set according to usage.</p>
<p>($1=185 escudos)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
